      "text": "We have  \n\\[\n(2^{1004}+5^{1005})^2-(2^{1004}-5^{1005})^2.\n\\]  \nUsing the difference of squares formula \\(a^2-b^2=(a-b)(a+b)\\):\n\nLet \\(a=2^{1004}+5^{1005}\\) and \\(b=2^{1004}-5^{1005}\\).  \nThen  \n\\[\na-b = (2^{1004}+5^{1005})-(2^{1004}-5^{1005}) = 2\\cdot 5^{1005},\n\\]  \n\\[\na+b = (2^{1004}+5^{1005})+(2^{1004}-5^{1005}) = 2\\cdot 2^{1004} = 2^{1005}.\n\\]  \n\nMultiply:  \n\\[\n(2\\cdot 5^{1005})(2^{1005}) = 2^{1006} \\cdot 5^{1005}.\n\\]  \n\nWe can rewrite \\(2^{1006} \\cdot 5^{1005}\\) as:  \n\\[\n2 \\cdot (2^{1005} \\cdot 5^{1005}) = 2 \\cdot 10^{1005}.\n\\]  \n\nBut the problem states the result is \\(k \\cdot 10^{1004}\\).  \nNote \\(2 \\cdot 10^{1005} = 20 \\cdot 10^{1004}\\).  \n\nThus \\(k = 20\\).\n\nThe answer is 20.",
